WEBVTT

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:32.500
Shoot!

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:36.690
Sharcrash!

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:40.690
Draciel!

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:45.240
With Team Psykick starting
to make suspicious moves

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:48.340
Ozma's team challenged us to a battle.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:50.600
Vanishing Moot!

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:00.190
Go, Shoot!

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:17.190
Darn...

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:35.360
Right after Max and Rei suffered a
bitter defeat by Mariam and Yusuf,

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:38.910
Takao has finally met
again with his rival, Ozma!

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:48.310
Ozma!

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:51.510
I finally found you!

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:53.510
You're Kinomiya!

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:05.200
Both Byakko and Genbu
have got a long way to go.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:06.430
Who're you?

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:07.540
Takao!

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:09.100
Max, Rei!

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:11.910
We had a look at
what they could do.

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:15.520
I thought they'd be a little
better than they actually were,

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:17.450
so I guess we overestimated them.

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:19.380
That means--

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:22.470
And we were so
close, too! Darn!

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:25.610
So close, and yet so
far away, am I right?

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:26.610
Right Yusuf?

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:27.660
What?!

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:29.650
We will win next time!

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:32.280
Whine as much as you like.

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:34.930
We'll take you on
whenever you want.

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:40.790
Rei, Max, I'm gonna get the
revenge you two couldn't get!

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:43.840
Will you accept my challenge, Ozma?

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:45.970
Bring it on!

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:58.110
Takao! Do it for us!

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:04.100
Let's do it! Go, Shoot!

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:05.250
Shoot!

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:12.880
Keep it up, Takao!

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:15.430
Here they are!

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:18.640
Ozma!

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:21.020
Takao is concentrating!

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:22.930
Dragoon, attack!

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:30.530
Why?! Why won't it move?

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:37.020
He's losing it.

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:39.730
What's your
next move, Kinomiya?

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:43.200
Once you attack
me head on, I'll...

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:54.290
I'm not falling for that.

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:56.500
That's it!
Good thinking, Takao!

00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:58.640
You've sharpened up a little.

00:04:58.850 --> 00:05:00.800
So how about this?!

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:11.890
Hang in there!
You can do it!

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:15.460
Just try it! Summon your
invisible Sacred Beast!

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:18.460
Go, Flash Leopard!

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:24.480
There it is!
His Sacred Beast!

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:27.460
Okay! Go, Dragoon!

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:40.240
Seiryu... How much of a
fight will he put up?

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:47.990
Darn it!

00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:56.850
How should I attack?

00:05:56.970 --> 00:05:59.700
Is that all you've
got after all?

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:01.220
Take this!

00:06:04.810 --> 00:06:05.890
Seiryu!

00:06:05.890 --> 00:06:06.820
Takao!

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:10.880
Hey, what's going on?

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:14.730
No! Seiryu can't hold
on much longer!

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:16.690
So that's a wrap?

00:06:16.690 --> 00:06:19.740
Seiryu's nothing
special either then?

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:21.680
Let's go, Yusuf.

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:23.940
Well, Takao Kinomiya?

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:25.710
Done already?

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:28.420
No, I don't want to lose!

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:30.720
If I screw up now, I'll...

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:33.990
Finish him off, Flash Leopard!

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:39.760
Darn...!

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:47.300
I can't lose!

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:49.200
Go, Dragoon!

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:51.450
Victory Tornado!

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:00.270
Keep it up, Takao!

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:03.360
Unbelievable! Where did all
that power come from?

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:05.690
Damn that Seiryu!

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:07.220
Back off.

00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:10.780
Pay attention and remember
what's happening here.

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:12.540
Remember their power.

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:14.640
Wrap it up, Dragoon!

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:25.910
I did it!

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:27.490
--Takao!

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:30.290
Good work out there!

00:07:30.290 --> 00:07:32.340
You finally got your
revenge on Ozma!

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:34.630
We finally beat him!

00:07:34.630 --> 00:07:37.530
Good job, Dragoon.
Good job, me!

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:39.950
How d'ya like that!

00:07:45.710 --> 00:07:48.290
We saw the whole thing, Ozma.

00:07:48.290 --> 00:07:51.720
Don't you think you played around
a little too much? I was getting bored!

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:55.650
It doesn't matter if you
won or lost, anyway.

00:07:55.650 --> 00:07:56.820
Back up!

00:07:56.820 --> 00:07:58.710
What do you mean
it doesn't matter?

00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:02.350
Yeah. I just wanted to
measure how much

00:08:02.980 --> 00:08:05.170
you and Seiryu have grown.

00:08:05.350 --> 00:08:06.400
What?!

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:08.250
Sounds like sour grapes!

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:10.960
Yeah!
That's bad sportsmanship!

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:15.940
I hate to say it Kinomiya,
but you and Seiryu

00:08:15.940 --> 00:08:17.980
have a lot more growing to do.

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:20.290
A lot more growing to do?

00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:21.570
What's that supposed to mean?

00:08:22.130 --> 00:08:24.470
Figure that out yourself.

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:32.530
Hey, Ozma!

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:35.780
What's his problem?

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:40.240
Why'd he have to say all that
just because Takao won?

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:41.790
Takao...

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:45.890
Seiryu... needs to grow...?

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:56.850
Talon, rotation rate 380.

00:08:56.850 --> 00:08:59.650
Center alignment, 90%.

00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:03.120
Good. Just a little more.
This time for sure...

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:05.030
It's approaching
critical rotation.

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:08.290
Come on out, my
digital Sacred Beast...

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:10.210
It has surpassed
critical rotation!

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:12.150
The energy is crossing over!

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:21.110
This is it! This is our
digital Sacred Beast!

00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:28.960
I have successfully created the world's
first scientifically engineered Sacred Beast!

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:44.850
Mr. Gideon, it's just as you see.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:48.480
The data of the four
Sacred Beasts is in here.

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:52.990
It can output the same level of
power that a real Sacred Beast can.

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:57.740
And now we just need a
Blader who can use it.

00:09:57.740 --> 00:09:59.810
Gerry! Come on out!

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:08.530
This is Gerry, an elite from
the Blader development rooms.

00:10:10.850 --> 00:10:14.390
I'm honored to be chosen
to wield a digital Sacred Beast.

00:10:16.020 --> 00:10:22.190
This arm attachment has all of the motion data from the BBA team

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:26.420
and their shooting
techniques input into it.

00:10:27.690 --> 00:10:30.450
Gerry, show Mr. Gideon an example.

00:10:30.450 --> 00:10:31.230
Yes, sir!

00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:33.700
That will not be necessary.

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:36.150
Mr. Gideon.

00:10:36.150 --> 00:10:38.950
Go out and try
this thing in town.

00:10:39.650 --> 00:10:41.780
To battle Takao Kinomiya?

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:43.000
Not quite.

00:10:45.670 --> 00:10:50.000
It's a skills test.
It doesn't matter who he fights.

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:55.280
I want to see how powerful the
digital Sacred Beast is in a battle.

00:10:55.450 --> 00:10:58.660
As you wish, Mr. Gideon.

00:11:00.770 --> 00:11:04.720
Lucky for us, there's a Beyblade tournament starting soon, Bro!

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:08.160
We should use this!

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:11.150
Well, Doctor?

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:12.510
Indeed.

00:11:12.760 --> 00:11:17.090
Go, Gerry. Prove that this
experiment will be a success.

00:11:17.090 --> 00:11:18.560
Leave it to me.

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:25.820
I expect nothing but good results.

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:37.960
"Bakuten Shoot Beyblade 2002"

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:50.070
Hey, Max and Takao! Keep those
legs moving and climb those stairs!

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:54.450
Jeez, why do we even
need to train like this?

00:11:54.450 --> 00:11:56.520
The basics start with endurance!

00:11:56.520 --> 00:11:59.390
There goes Hiromi, going
on about the basics again...

00:11:59.390 --> 00:12:03.770
You guys need to polish your
fundamentals if you want revenge!

00:12:03.770 --> 00:12:06.010
It sure sucks to
hear it though...

00:12:06.170 --> 00:12:09.890
Hold on, Hiromi!
I got my revenge!

00:12:09.890 --> 00:12:15.280
Then you need to beat Ozma so badly
that he can't talk you down again!

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:16.650
Keep it up!

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:21.920
C'mon, can't you do something
about this, Kyoujyu?

00:12:25.570 --> 00:12:29.390
Please, just leave me
behind and go on ahead!

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:30.990
I'm out...

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:39.520
Here you go, Takao.

00:12:40.090 --> 00:12:41.700
Thanks.

00:12:44.770 --> 00:12:46.860
What's got you daydreaming?

00:12:46.860 --> 00:12:49.640
What did he mean about
us having more growing to do?

00:12:50.390 --> 00:12:56.000
Ozma said that Seiryu and
I have a lot more ahead of us.

00:12:56.640 --> 00:12:58.980
But what the heck am
I supposed to do?

00:12:59.140 --> 00:13:01.030
So it was bugging you.

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:02.930
Definitely.

00:13:02.930 --> 00:13:06.230
Why would he say that
to me in the first place?

00:13:06.710 --> 00:13:08.700
It's strange.

00:13:08.990 --> 00:13:10.010
Kyoujyu.

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:13.640
I don't think that Ozma's group,
unlike the Psykicks,

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:16.980
is trying to take away
your Sacred Beasts.

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:19.410
But he was oddly supportive.

00:13:19.680 --> 00:13:22.690
Like what if there's
an ulterior motive?

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:23.650
Like what?

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:25.180
I don't know.

00:13:25.180 --> 00:13:28.180
You guys are overthinking it.

00:13:28.190 --> 00:13:29.700
What do you mean, Max?

00:13:29.860 --> 00:13:35.860
Having a lot more growing to do means that Seiryu still<b> has room for improvement!</b>

00:13:35.860 --> 00:13:36.880
I get it!

00:13:36.880 --> 00:13:40.300
So Seiryu can still get stronger!

00:13:40.300 --> 00:13:43.620
Which means we can, too!

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:48.060
He's so simple.

00:13:48.060 --> 00:13:52.450
If they gave us that advice, does that mean they're on our side?

00:13:52.450 --> 00:13:54.260
Ozma's team?

00:13:55.510 --> 00:13:58.000
I thought they were
our enemies, but...

00:13:58.190 --> 00:14:03.120
I don't know who's on our
side and who isn't anymore...

00:14:03.350 --> 00:14:05.420
We shouldn't let our guard down.

00:14:06.460 --> 00:14:07.340
Kai.

00:14:07.340 --> 00:14:11.010
Drop your guard and your
Sacred Beast will be snatched away.

00:14:11.010 --> 00:14:12.380
I've got that feeling.

00:14:12.380 --> 00:14:14.960
They're not get snatched
away without a fight.

00:14:15.300 --> 00:14:18.050
We've fought together for so long.

00:14:18.050 --> 00:14:19.630
I'm not giving you to anyone!

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:20.520
--Yeah!

00:14:23.140 --> 00:14:25.960
So let's continue our training!

00:14:44.260 --> 00:14:47.290
We'll send you everything you
need to know through that.

00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:50.750
Just you watch.
I'm gonna blow 'em away.

00:14:51.170 --> 00:14:55.220
I see. So you battled
with Ozma's team?

00:14:55.220 --> 00:14:56.000
Yes.

00:14:56.320 --> 00:14:58.970
We have no idea
on who they are,

00:14:58.970 --> 00:15:04.320
if they're with, against us,
or where to even see them.

00:15:04.320 --> 00:15:06.990
So we thought you
might know something.

00:15:06.990 --> 00:15:11.590
As I've mentioned earlier, we have
information from eyewitnesses...

00:15:11.590 --> 00:15:14.690
However we know nothing
other than that. I'm sorry.

00:15:15.790 --> 00:15:20.900
I guess we'll have to find out
what Ozma wants by ourselves.

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:24.180
But what if they catch
us off guard again?

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:27.360
That's what I'm
worried about, too.

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:30.090
And not just Ozma's team,

00:15:30.090 --> 00:15:35.590
but those radical scientists are
challenging you to unfair battles.

00:15:35.590 --> 00:15:40.870
We want to arrange a fair
battle as soon as possible.

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:44.570
Chairman, it's time to go.

00:15:44.570 --> 00:15:46.100
Oh, that's right.

00:15:46.700 --> 00:15:51.520
I have to make an appearance at
a small tournament in town today.

00:15:51.520 --> 00:15:55.360
Would you like to join
me just to watch?

00:15:56.110 --> 00:15:57.970
Really? Awesome!

00:15:57.970 --> 00:16:01.730
I don't care how big the
tourney is, as long as I can battle!

00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:03.870
I am so in!

00:16:03.870 --> 00:16:05.820
I thought he said
we'd just watch.

00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:08.500
That was my intention, but...

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:11.770
Sweet! This'll be a
good change of pace!

00:16:11.770 --> 00:16:20.200
Today's tournament at the station is
starting to heat up in the semi-finals!

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:24.650
These are the four Bladers
who survived intense battles!

00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:26.430
Come on stage!

00:16:30.640 --> 00:16:34.700
Is now a good time to bring
out the digital Sacred Beast?

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:36.390
Doctor.

00:16:36.390 --> 00:16:38.690
Knock yourself out.
Fight and summon it.

00:16:38.690 --> 00:16:43.140
The other kids won't be able to tell it's a Sacred Beast anyway.

00:16:43.250 --> 00:16:45.010
Do you copy, Gerry?

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:46.900
Awesome.

00:16:48.740 --> 00:16:49.790
Ready?

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:50.910
Three!

00:16:50.910 --> 00:16:52.110
Two!

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:52.990
One!

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:55.010
Go, Shoot!

00:16:55.010 --> 00:16:56.400
Shoot!

00:16:59.590 --> 00:17:02.400
Wow! An intense attack
right out of the gate!

00:17:02.400 --> 00:17:05.090
This is a battle fit for the semi-finals!

00:17:05.090 --> 00:17:07.090
That's it! Keep up the attack!

00:17:08.230 --> 00:17:11.300
Playtime is over!

00:17:11.740 --> 00:17:14.100
Talon!

00:17:19.580 --> 00:17:22.580
Gerry's Bey is
approaching critical rotation.

00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:25.970
Mr. Gideon, please watch closely.

00:17:25.970 --> 00:17:30.650
An ordinary Bey is as good as dust in
the wind against a digital Sacred Beast.

00:17:30.650 --> 00:17:33.280
The digital Sacred Beast is taking form.

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:38.740
Rise, my digital Sacred Beast!

00:17:47.970 --> 00:17:51.830
What's going on?
A mysterious hurricane has...!

00:17:53.250 --> 00:17:54.510
There it is!

00:17:58.080 --> 00:18:00.930
What's going on?
What's all the fuss about?

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:02.180
Takao!

00:18:03.900 --> 00:18:05.280
What happened?

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:07.500
We just got here.

00:18:10.700 --> 00:18:12.200
This response!

00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:15.150
It's a Sacred Beast!
A Sacred Beast is on the attack!

00:18:15.150 --> 00:18:16.220
A what?!

00:18:16.220 --> 00:18:17.720
A Sacred Beast?

00:18:18.050 --> 00:18:19.090
But how?

00:18:20.310 --> 00:18:21.300
Takao!

00:18:26.980 --> 00:18:29.420
Yes! Keep going!

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:31.300
Raise as much hell as you like!

00:18:36.180 --> 00:18:37.300
What's that?

00:18:41.300 --> 00:18:43.900
I've never seen that before!

00:18:44.160 --> 00:18:47.200
It appears to be an
artificial Sacred Beast!

00:18:47.200 --> 00:18:48.420
Artificial?!

00:18:48.650 --> 00:18:51.410
I remember seeing the
composition of this wavelength.

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:54.310
It's exactly the
same as Psykick's data!

00:18:54.310 --> 00:18:55.910
Psykick's...?!

00:19:02.250 --> 00:19:05.930
The digital Sacred Beast has surpassed
critical rotation and has gone berserk!

00:19:05.930 --> 00:19:07.220
What?!

00:19:10.060 --> 00:19:12.860
Doctor... what is the meaning of this?

00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:15.630
The data should be perfect!

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:18.560
It's exactly the same
as the BBA team's data!

00:19:18.560 --> 00:19:21.720
In theory, it shouldn't
go berserk at all!

00:19:23.740 --> 00:19:30.090
On second thought, there must be something about
the four Sacred Beasts we have yet to figure out...

00:19:31.680 --> 00:19:34.100
The digital Sacred Beast
is not responding!

00:19:34.640 --> 00:19:36.510
Hey, you Psykick creep!

00:19:36.700 --> 00:19:39.210
I don't know you are
but I'm taking you out!

00:19:39.210 --> 00:19:41.380
Wait! This is dangerous, Takao!

00:19:41.380 --> 00:19:43.550
Interesting. Bring it on!

00:19:43.550 --> 00:19:47.350
I will show you the power
of my digital Sacred Beast!

00:19:54.050 --> 00:19:56.700
What's going on?
What's happening?!

00:20:02.900 --> 00:20:04.290
No way!

00:20:04.560 --> 00:20:06.620
What in the world...

00:20:06.980 --> 00:20:09.360
Error detected in the energy output!

00:20:09.360 --> 00:20:11.200
It's emitting powerful shockwaves!

00:20:12.550 --> 00:20:16.680
I see that it was not quite
prepared for practical use.

00:20:16.680 --> 00:20:20.370
Please, wait!
This is merely a fluke...

00:20:20.370 --> 00:20:22.820
Take care of this immediately.

00:20:23.030 --> 00:20:29.010
Show me once the digital
Sacred Beasts are truly complete.

00:20:34.060 --> 00:20:36.910
The shockwaves are
entering the danger zone!

00:20:37.820 --> 00:20:40.820
Get Gerry and Talon out of there!

00:20:40.820 --> 00:20:44.420
I will find the cause of this!

00:21:06.400 --> 00:21:07.250
Floor it!

00:21:07.250 --> 00:21:08.510
Aye aye, Bro!

00:21:09.350 --> 00:21:11.090
I remember them!

00:21:11.090 --> 00:21:12.050
Stop!

00:21:27.150 --> 00:21:30.290
What are those
Psykicks up to now...?

00:22:59.170 --> 00:23:01.920
The digital Sacred Beasts
have finally appeared!

00:23:01.920 --> 00:23:05.380
The four Sacred Beasts will have tougher and tougher battles from here on out!

00:23:05.380 --> 00:23:09.920
Huh? Hiromi says she wants to
see the Sacred Beasts, too?

00:23:09.920 --> 00:23:11.740
What do we do, Chairman?

00:23:11.740 --> 00:23:15.330
If Hiromi gets ticked off, the digital Sacred Beasts will be the least of our problems!

00:23:15.330 --> 00:23:18.140
I think something amazing
will happen in the next episode!

00:23:18.140 --> 00:23:20.130
You won't want to miss it!
